// SigningSiblings groups the services that sign with the same SigV4 name, for
// the names more than one service shares.
//
// AWS splits a data plane, runtime, or successor version into its own SDK client
// but leaves it signing with the parent's name — mediastore-data signs
// "mediastore", service-catalog-appregistry signs "servicecatalog". ServiceIDs
// can only answer with one of them, so every other member of the group would be
// registered and then routed to the wrong provider for any caller that addresses
